        {
          "id": "RUSTSEC-2026-0348",
          "package": "rustls",
          "versions": [
            "0.23.45"
          ],
          "notes": [
            "ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0348",
            "Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0348",
            "The built-in Brotli certificate decompressor (enabled by the non-default\n`brotli` crate feature) bounded the size of the decompressed output, but\naccepted a peer-selected history window. Brotli's large-window extension was\nenabled, so a five-byte header could cause an allocation of 1 GiB. A peer can\nabort a process whose allocator cannot satisfy that request.\n\nNo trusted certificate is required by the attacker. Affected configurations are:\n\n- clients that enable the `brotli` feature and connect to a malicious server, and\n- servers that enable the `brotli` feature and request client certificates.\n\nApplications that do not enable the `brotli` feature are not affected.",
            "Announcement: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/pull/3297",
            "Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.46 (try `cargo update -p rustls`)"
          ],
